amera.\par \par \uc2 BRAVINDER: Yes.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: And so, that officer initially started assisting with chest compressions of Mr. Floyd.\par \par \uc2 BRAVINDER: Yes. I wasn`t in back when that would have happened, but --\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Your partner was?\par \par \uc2 BRAVINDER: Yes.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: And he would probably be the person to ask about that?\par \par \uc2 BRAVINDER: Yes. I would have been. You can see in the footage we watched, but I was there for a brief period and then went to the front to drive.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: All right, so you`ve seen the body-worn camera footage from inside of the ambulance?\par \par \uc2 BRAVINDER: Yes, I`ve seen a good amount of it. I don`t know if I`ve seen all of it but --\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: OK. You describe the Lucas Device putting on -- or that you describe that Lucas Device that does the chest compressions, right?\par \par \uc2 BRAVINDER: Yes.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: It was your partner that was putting that on with that police officer, correct?\par \par \uc2 BRAVINDER: No, I was putting that on with the police officer.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: OK. So, you and he -- so, you were in the ambulance when the officer was performing chest compressions?\par \par \uc2 BRAVINDER: Yes, after I pulled over on 36 and Park and gotten to the back, he would have been doing chest compressions.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: So, the first thing he did was load Mr. Floyd in to the vehicle, you drive to 36 in Park, right?\par \par \uc2 BRAVINDER: Yes.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: And while you drove that distance to 36 and Park, the officer was in the back with your partner performing chest compressions?\par \par \uc2 BRAVINDER: I would assume I wasn`t in back.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: And then -- but when you got into the back to assist your partner, that`s what you observed was the officer performing chest compressions?\par \p