FIED MALE: And let me ask you one question that I forgot to ask you about the initial call. The initial call you said was code two, correct? And it got upgraded to code three, meaning lights and sirens.\par \par \uc2 BRAVINDER: Correct.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: And that was about a minute and a half after the initial call, agreed?\par \par \uc2 BRAVINDER: Based on what I looked at the times, from what I`ve seen after, it looked like it was about a minute and a half.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: And the time from when it got upgraded until you arrived on scene, would you agree that was about six, six and a half minutes, something like that?\par \par \uc2 BRAVINDER: I believe it was close to that, yes.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: OK. And then it was you added -- was it you who added fire to the call or was it your partner?\par \par \uc2 BRAVINDER: I believe -- I can`t say for sure who said it first. I think my -- I believe my partner said it first over the radio.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: OK. And that`s when fire gets dispatched and they ultimately -- you understand and went to Cup Foods first?\par \par \uc2 BRAVINDER: I heard that afterwards, yes.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: OK, you didn`t know it at the time?\par \par \uc2 BRAVINDER: No, when I -- as we were moving to 36 on Park, I went over the radio and told our dispatch that we were going to be moving to have fire meet us there.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: OK. And then the information you had as you were initially responding was that there was a mouth injury, correct?\par \par \uc2 BRAVINDER: Yes.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: And that there was information that the male may be intoxicated or impaired?\par \par \uc2 BRAVINDER: Yes. There was some notes about -- I can`t remember the exact wording, but there`s something about substance use or -- I can`t remember if it said narcotic or substance use concern. And then, there was a note saying, he was on top of a vehicle.\par \par 